Mon Nov  9 15:33:19 UTC 2026 - Danilo Spinella <danilo.spinella@suse.com>

- Update to 0.9.31:
  * Bugfix/issue 90 windows perf
- Update to 0.9.30:
  * ConcurrentTimedRotatingFileHandler no longer creates the log
    file in its constructor.
  * Remove a duplicate stale-file check from each write. On a local
    disk this cuts the time per write by about 13% when maxBytes is
    set, for both handlers.
  * 0.9.30
  * Mark Python 3.15 as supported.
  * Fix permission race window between file create and chmod, when
    the chmod and/or owner kwargs are configured.
  * Fix lost records when a process opens a lock file or log file
    that another user owns, with chmod or owner configured.
- Update to 0.9.29:
  * Fix race conditions when a handler created before fork() is
    used by multiple child processes.
  * Depend on portalocker >= 2.6.0 instead of 1.6.0. Earlier
    versions of portalocker on Windows can be problematic.
  * Add finalize_handler_configuration() hook to
    ConcurrentTimedRotatingFileHandler to allow customization of
    the handler before the first rollover.
- Update to 0.9.28:
  * 0.9.28
  * Fix missing a rollover when the app was shutdown during the
    scheduled time.
  * Fix NameError when logging during Python shutdown.
- Update to 0.9.27:
  * Adds deprecation warning to queue.py setup_logging_queues().
  * Fixes - issues cleaning up old rotation files
  * Fixes - issues around syncing time to rollover
  * Stop using this and just use regular synchronous logging calls
    (the standard handlers)
- Update to 0.9.26:
  * GitHub Actions no longer supports runners for automated testing
    under Python 3.6 and 3.7.
  * Ensure required packages like black are installed in "dev mode"
    (pip install -e .[dev]).
  * 0.9.26
  * Significant performance improvements, especially on the POSIX
    side.
  * This is mainly from keeping the file handles open for both the
    log file and the lock file, reducing system calls and overhead.
  * You can revert to the old behavior by setting
    keep_file_open=False in the constructor. The default is True.
- Update to 0.9.25:
  * Updates to use pyproject.toml with a few other features
  * Fixes: ConcurrentTimedRotatingFileHandler rotating gzip fil…
  * Initial support for typing
- Update to 0.9.24:
  * see
    https://github.com/Preston-Landers/concurrent-log-handler/releases/tag/0.9.24
- Update to 0.9.23:
  * 0.9.23
  * Begin requiring Python 3.6 or higher.
  * Fix - don't fail when setting owner on Windows, though it will
    have no effect.
- Update to 0.9.23-alpha-1:
  * see
    https://github.com/Preston-Landers/concurrent-log-handler/releases/tag/0.9.23-alpha-1
- Update to 0.9.22:
  * see
    https://github.com/Preston-Landers/concurrent-log-handler/releases/tag/0.9.22
- Update to 0.9.21:
  * Added new optional parameter "lock_file_directory"
  * Creates given directory, if it does not exist.
  * Writes lock file into given directory, instead next to the
    logging file itself.
  * Useful when the log files reside in a cloud synced folder like
    Dropbox, Google Drive, OneDrive, etc. Sometimes these do not
    work correctly with the lock files.
  * Fix not replacing the last file (greatest backup number) when
    rotating. Thanks tzongw.
  * PR#52
- Update to 0.9.20:
  * see
    https://github.com/Preston-Landers/concurrent-log-handler/releases/tag/0.9.20
- Fix the stress test path in %check after the tests moved to
  tests/
- Run the pytest suite in %check since stresstest.py fails as a
  script
- Remove the leading shebang line from the installed
  concurrent_log_handler module

